# Kavis — X11 + Openbox + terminal (stage 1)
#
# Our own components (panel, greeter, settings) do not exist yet; this
# list sets up the "boots and the graphical interface opens" skeleton.

# --- X server ---
xserver-xorg
xserver-xorg-core
xserver-xorg-input-all
xserver-xorg-video-all
xinit
x11-xserver-utils
x11-utils

# --- window manager ---
openbox

# --- login manager (to be replaced by kavis-greeter in stage 5) ---
lightdm
lightdm-gtk-greeter

# --- terminal (LXDE family: GTK3, light, same team as pcmanfm) ---
# tilix: the only compiled candidate that meets the item 40 "split
# window" requirement (lxterminal has tabs but no splitting; terminator
# is Python).
tilix

# xsettingsd: live theme/scale switching (item 38/10) — Settings writes
# Net/ThemeName and Xft/DPI and sends SIGHUP; GTK applications update
# without a restart.
xsettingsd

# lxpolkit: session polkit agent — pkexec dialogs (nemo "open as
# administrator", item 64 repair) NEVER open without the agent.
lxpolkit

# --- compositor (stage 4) ---
# Rounded corners, shadows and smooth transitions are drawn only with
# compositing. Without picom, windows with transparent edges like the
# power menu get a black frame around them. The xrender backend is used:
# it also works in virtual machines without 3D acceleration and uses
# little RAM.
picom

# --- wallpaper (stage 2; the panel takes over in stage 4) ---
# xwallpaper instead of feh: does one job, ~50 KB, leaves no background
# process.
xwallpaper

# --- minimal support so GTK3 works (required since Recommends is off) ---
adwaita-icon-theme
gtk-update-icon-cache
librsvg2-common
fonts-dejavu-core
fonts-liberation2

# --- UI font (v0.4-test4 feedback A1) ---
# fonts-inter: the system UI face at 10pt. Chosen over the previous
# DejaVu Sans because DejaVu is a text face — at UI sizes its low
# x-height and heavy stems are what made the VM screenshots look
# "pixelated". Inter was drawn for screen UI at exactly this size.
# fonts-noto-core: the fallback for scripts Inter does not cover
# (Cyrillic beyond the basics, Greek, Arabic...). Kavis is meant to be
# translated, so a missing-glyph box is a real failure, not cosmetics.
# Rendering policy (slight hinting + subpixel) is in
# includes.chroot/etc/fonts/local.conf.
fonts-inter
fonts-noto-core

# NOTE (after item 3): the Python + PyGObject stack was REMOVED — the
# panel is now a compiled Vala binary, no component on the ISO depends on
# Python. If a user application returns to Python later, its
# dependencies will come from that package's Depends field.

# --- quick settings backends (item 37) ---
# The panel probes these tools at runtime; if absent the related button
# is hidden.
# rfkill: Bluetooth on/off (hardware switch interface, ~100 KB)
# xsct: night mode — X color temperature, tiny single-purpose tool (sct is not in the trixie archive)
# brightnessctl: brightness; solves the permission problem with udev rules
rfkill
xsct
brightnessctl

# --- desktop icons (item 6) ---
# nemo-desktop is inside the nemo package; Group E will use nemo as the
# file manager anyway (item 39) — bringing it early is not double work.
nemo

# --- panel DBus bridge (item 55/7) ---
# The Openbox shortcuts call the running panel with gdbus (W-Tab
# overview, W-v clipboard history). libglib2.0-bin contains gdbus; it
# does not come by itself with Recommends off.
libglib2.0-bin

# --- clipboard history paste + emoji rendering (item 7) ---
# xdotool: on Win+V presses the selected item into the focused window
# with Ctrl+V.
# fonts-noto-color-emoji: so the emoji picker's cells draw emoji, not
# boxes.
xdotool
fonts-noto-color-emoji

# --- touchpad gestures (next-tasks 6g) ---
# libinput-tools: `libinput debug-events` — our own gesture reader
# /usr/lib/kavis/kavis-gestures reads it (libinput-gestures and touchegg
# are NOT in the trixie archive). The user is in the `input` group
# (bootappend) — device read permission comes from there.
libinput-tools

# --- tray USB tool (item 3 fix) ---
# udisksctl: safely remove — thanks to polkit the live user can unmount
# and power off without root. Does not come by itself through the
# nemo/gvfs chain with Recommends off; written explicitly.
udisks2

# --- screenshot and screen recording (item 29 + Group D 5) ---
# Frozen frame + dimming + selectors are now kavis-tools' own code
# (flameshot and slop removed); ffmpeg stays for x11grab video recording.
ffmpeg

# C4 (v0.4-test1): the start menu on a lone Win key press — openbox
# cannot bind a modifier on its own; xcape turns a Super_L tap into F13,
# rc.xml forwards F13 to the panel.
xcape
